{"name":"Kissed by a Zombies","hex":"#b15363","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kissed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of kiss"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kissed"},{"term":"zombies","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of zombie"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zombies"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kissed","blocks":[{"text":"Kissed is a 1996 Canadian romantic/erotic drama film directed and co-written by Lynne Stopkewich, based on Barbara Gowdy's short story \"We So Seldom Look on Love\". It premiered at the Toronto International Film Festival on September 7, 1996."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/18/Kissed_%281996_movie_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kissed","wikidata":"Q939844"},{"title":"Zombie","blocks":[{"text":"A zombie is a legendary undead being created through the reanimation of a cadaver, a corporeal manifestation of the revenant type. In modern popular culture, zombies often appear in horror genre works. The term comes from Haitian folklore, in which a zombie is a dead body reanimated through magic by a bokor sorcerer. Modern media depictions of the reanimation of the dead often do not involve magic but rather science fictional methods such as fungi, radiation, gases, infection, diseases, plants, bacteria, viruses, etc."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Zombie_haiti_ill_artlibre_jnl.png/330px-Zombie_haiti_ill_artlibre_jnl.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zombie","wikidata":"Q9406"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Barbara_Gowdy_-_Eden_Mills_Writers_Festival_-_2017_%28DanH-9388%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Barbara_Gowdy_-_Eden_Mills_Writers_Festival_-_2017_%28DanH-9388%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Barbara_Gowdy_-_Eden_Mills_Writers_Festival_-_2017_%28DanH-9388%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Barbara_Gowdy_-_Eden_Mills_Writers_Festival_-_2017_%28DanH-9388%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"We So Seldom Look on Love\", a 1992 short story about a necrophile written by Barbara Gowdy (pictured) was Lynne Stopkewich's main inspiration for Kissed","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarbara_Gowdy_-_Eden_Mills_Writers_Festival_-_2017_(DanH-9388)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/PER51895_061.jpg/500px-PER51895_061.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/PER51895_061.jpg/1280px-PER51895_061.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/PER51895_061.jpg/500px-PER51895_061.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The 1974 film Effi Briest, directed by Rainer Werner Fassbinder (pictured), was an influence on Stopkewich's symbolic use of white light in Kissed","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APER51895_061.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Zombies_NightoftheLivingDead.jpg/500px-Zombies_NightoftheLivingDead.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Zombies_NightoftheLivingDead.jpg/1280px-Zombies_NightoftheLivingDead.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Zombies_NightoftheLivingDead.jpg/500px-Zombies_NightoftheLivingDead.jpg?u